Chapter: EffectLaunderHof
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Higher-order effect laundering. apply-pure declares a pure function
 parameter (Integer -> Integer). leaky is Integer -> [Console]
 Integer. Passing leaky where a pure function is required used to
 compile clean and RUN the I/O, because function-type unification
 stripped the effect row. The per-argument effect check now rejects
 it: the actual argument's Console effect is not permitted by the
 parameter's pure type (CDX2031).

Section: Definitions

  apply-pure : (Integer -> Integer), Integer -> Integer
  apply-pure (f) (x) = f x

  leaky : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  leaky (n) = act
    print-line-uni "side channel"
    n + 1
  end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (apply-pure leaky 41))
  end
